An \code{sf} object with point geometry in EPSG 26917 (NAD 1983 UTM Zone 17N), sorted by incident date and time. Columns include \code{category}, \code{location_block}, \code{occ_num} (occurrence number) and \code{incident_datetime}.
}
\description{
Reads police-reported incidents from the Windsor Police Service Incident Dashboard. This is a separate source from the City of Windsor open data portal: it is a public ArcGIS FeatureServer hosted by Windsor Police Service, not one of the 227 datasets in \code{\link{windsor_datasets}}. It covers the City of Windsor and the Town of Amherstburg, for the last two years, updated daily.
}
\details{
Locations are anonymised to the block, for example "2200 BLOCK 2ND CONCESSION RD N". Some incidents and incident types are not displayed, for privacy or investigative reasons, and the police note that all map visualisations should be considered approximate. Motor vehicle collisions are not included in this feed. The "Traffic" category is police traffic incidents, not a collision file.
